  -- 2026-09-29: Tier A row 6
  STRUCT('FIRST WEST OF ENGLAND', '00025088', 'accepted', DATE '2026-09-29', 'TIER A, USER DECISION, 2026-09-29. Basis: the payer own coding plus a rule-resolved spelling from an independent payer. The Department for Transport is the only payer of this spelling, 28 payments, GBP 18,728,940.74, every one coded as private-sector subsidy under its public-transport directorate -- bus-operator funding, matching the candidate SIC 49319 - Other urban, suburban or metropolitan passenger land transport (not underground, metro or similar). Bristol City Council pays FIRST WEST OF ENGLAND LTD (102 rows), which resolves BY RULE at tier 2, high confidence, to the same 00025088. The Department for Transport also pays other First bus operating companies under names that resolve by rule. Single candidate, score 1; the only near rival is non-trading. Not an established class (the bridge crosses payers); decided per row.'),
  -- 2026-09-29: Tier A row 7
  STRUCT('XEROX U K LTD', '00330754', 'accepted', DATE '2026-09-29', 'TIER A, USER DECISION, 2026-09-29. A demoted tier-1 row: the buyer-stated 00330754 is registered as XEROX (UK) LIMITED, and the payer spells it XEROX U K -- the demotion is a normalisation artefact (spaced initials), not a different company. Basis: Ministry of Justice is the only payer, 81 rows, GBP 18,657,155.04, of which 99.23% is coded print or reprographics, matching SIC 46660 - Wholesale of other office machinery and equipment; 3 other payers pay XEROX UK LTD, which resolves BY RULE at tier 2 to 00330754; 9 Contracts Finder awards state 00330754. Of the 2 stating 00575914 XEROX LIMITED, one names only Xerox and the other names Xerox (UK) Limited while stating another company number -- self-contradictory (the Eversheds precedent).'),
  -- 2026-09-29: Tier A row 8
  STRUCT('GO NORTH EAST', '02057284', 'accepted', DATE '2026-09-29', 'TIER A, USER DECISION, 2026-09-29. Basis: the payer own coding plus its rule-resolved pattern for the same group. The Department for Transport is the only payer of this spelling, 23 payments, GBP 16,197,710.54, every one coded as private-sector subsidy under its public-transport directorate -- bus-operator funding, matching the candidate SIC 49319 - Other urban, suburban or metropolitan passenger land transport (not underground, metro or similar). The same payer pays two sibling Go-Ahead operating companies under names that resolve BY RULE (GO NORTH WEST LTD tier 2 08205871; GO SOUTH COAST LTD tier 1 03949597). The candidate was named GO GATESHEAD LIMITED until 2007-05-22, before every payment. Single candidate, score 1; no other register entry carries the name at the group address. Not an established class; decided per row.'),
  -- 2026-09-29: Tier A row 9
  STRUCT('CHEVRON TRAFFIC MANAGEMENT', '03316774', 'accepted', DATE '2026-09-29', 'TIER A, USER DECISION, confirmed by the user 2026-09-29 under the per-row protocol. Queue-row value GBP 15,469,635.90, the pre-rename spelling only. Basis: one Department for Transport payment stream under two spellings -- CHEVRON TRAFFIC MANAGEMENT, 168 rows from 2024-03-08 to 2024-07-24; then CHEVRON TRAFFIC MANAGEMENT LTD, 260 rows from 2024-08-15 to 2025-02-28, which resolves BY RULE at tier 2, high confidence, to 03316774. The windows are contiguous without overlap, and all 3 expense codes of the first spelling (Operations Directorate) recur under the second. Manchester City Council also pays the Ltd spelling (41 rows). Candidate SIC 52290 - Other transportation support activities; single candidate. The same-payer bridge class, decided per row as Tier A.'),
